Package: BPVS
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Panel Variable Selection with Regularized Horseshoe Priors
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pathairat", "Pastpipatkul", email = "p.pastpipatkul@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Htwe", "Ko", email = "htweko@example.com", role = "aut"))
Description: Bayesian Panel Variable Selection (BPVS) for balanced panels. A regularized
    horseshoe (continuous spike-and-slab) prior is placed on the slope coefficients while
    unit-specific heterogeneity is handled either by fixed effects (unit dummies, BPVS-FE)
    or by random intercepts (BPVS-RE). The package computes posterior inclusion
    probabilities (PIPs), variable rankings, WAIC and Bayesian R-squared, and Bayesian and
    frequentist Hausman comparisons between the two panel specifications. Estimation is
    implemented with 'brms' on 'Stan'.
